1 RIN 028ef59b-ed15-4d3c-a079-6491ce337aed
1 DATE 1711
1 _DSCR York Peculiar's Index on Findmypast.
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription>Brief summary: 
2 CONT Richard Farrer clothier of Pudsey [974] 1704 Aug. 29 Richard Farrer of Pudsey, Yorks., clothier. I give to Phoebe my wife a third part of my real estate for life &amp; 5/-. To my son Richard Farrer the messuage wherein I now live with the land ther
2 CONC eto belonging. To my son William Farrer one messuage and land in Pudsey which I bought of William Kellett. To my daughter Saran wife of William Fenton one dwellinghouse a cottage and shop now in possession of the said William Fenton and £10. To Joh
2 CONC n Pearson and Elizabeth his wife my daughter £40. To John Wood and Mary his wife my daughter 5/-. The residue to Phoebe Farrar my daughter. executrix. Supervisors, John Wood and John Pearson my sons-in-law. Witnesses Samuel Scott, Robert Telford, W
2 CONC m .Hepton. (Pr. 8 Jan. 17l1.) (York, Original Will.)</transcription></metadataxml>
